 "etapas": [
  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Verb and preposition",
     "texto": [
      "**Depender de** (to depend on), **contribuir para** (to contribute to), **insistir em** (to insist on), **assistir a** (to watch / attend, in European Portuguese): **O resultado depende dos dados** (the result depends on the data); **Assistimos ao debate** (we watched the debate). The preposition is kept before a noun and, in many cases, before an infinitive: **Insistiu em participar** (he / she insisted on taking part)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Before choosing",
     "texto": [
      "The Portuguese preposition doesn't always match the Spanish one. Learn each construction with the verb and check the meaning: **assistir a um filme** means to watch a film; **assistir alguém** can mean to help or to assist someone."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
